	<h1>
		Submissions
	</h1>

	<div class="cmp_notification">
					This journal is not accepting submissions at this time.
			</div>

		<div class="author_guidelines" id="authorGuidelines">
		<h2>
			Author Guidelines
					</h2>
		<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Brief Instructions for Author</strong><br> 1. Before submitting your manuscript, please read our <a href="http://journal.scadindependent.org/index.php/jipeuradeun/authorguidelines" target="_blank">online guide</a>&nbsp;How to increase online readership of your article<br>2. Fluent, comprehensible, and correct use of English is the main criteria. The authors should ensure that the manuscript has no linguistic problems. Otherwise, it is rejected in the pre-assessment. Proofreading is strongly advised.<br>3. To submit a new manuscript, click on "<strong>New Submission</strong>" in the link.&nbsp;To continue a submission already in progress, follow the step-by-step process requested, and do not forget to click "<strong>Save and Continue</strong>". Follow the requested process until it is finished.<br>4. If you are submitting a revision and the option has expired, please contact the editor to ask for an extension.&nbsp;<strong><a href="http://journal.scadindependent.org/index.php/jipeuradeun/authorguidelines" target="_blank">Read and Download Author Guidelines</a></strong></p>
	</div>
	
			<div class="submission_checklist">
			<h2>
				Submission Preparation Checklist
							</h2>
			<p>All submissions must meet the following requirements.</p><ul><li>I guarantee that the manuscript submitted is the author`s original work. And I also guarantee that the manuscript is being submitted solely to the JIP only and that it has never been published in any publication, that no publication is being requested, that it is not being submitted elsewhere, or that it is not being considered by other media.</li><li>I guarantee that the authors/contributors listed on the title page will follow all stages in the evaluation and publishing process at the JIP.</li><li>We accept that the Editorial decisions over the acceptance or rejection or in the event of any breach of the Ethics Statement in the JIP being discovered of retraction are final.</li><li>If we violate these provisions, then we are willing to accept all the consequences that apply in accordance with the legislation and publication ethics (we have also attached the Author Statement Form to this manuscript).</li><li>The manuscript is written in a sequence, consisting of the title, author's name, abstract, keywords, and content of the manuscript according to IMRAD guidelines (Introduction, Method, Result, Discussion, Conclusion, and Bibliography), and has been following the journal template, which contains approximately 4.000–7.000 words including text, all tables, figures, notes, references, and appendices intended for publication, with the following to the author's guidelines for this journal.</li></ul>
		</div>
	
			                            
	
			<div class="copyright_notice">
			<h2>
				Copyright Notice
							</h2>
			<p style="text-align: justify;"><em>Authors who publish with this journal agree to the following terms: (1) Authors retain copyright and grant the journal right of first publication with the work simultaneously licensed under a&nbsp;<a href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License</a>&nbsp;<strong>(CC-BY-SA)</strong>&nbsp;that allows others to share the work with an acknowledgment of the work's authorship and initial publication in this journal; (2) Authors are able to enter into separate, additional contractual arrangements for the non-exclusive distribution of the journal's published version of the work (e.g., post it to an institutional repository or publish it in a book), with an acknowledgment of its initial publication in this journal; (3) Authors are permitted and encouraged to post their work online (e.g., in institutional repositories or on their website) prior to and during the submission process, as it can lead to productive exchanges, as well as earlier and greater citation of published work&nbsp;(<a href="http://opcit.eprints.org/oacitation-biblio.html" target="_blank">See The Effect of Open Access</a>).&nbsp;</em></p>
		</div>
	
		<div class="privacy_statement" id="privacyStatement">
		<h2>
			Privacy Statement
					</h2>
		The names and email addresses entered in this journal site will be used exclusively for the stated purposes of this journal and will not be made available for any other purpose or to any other party.
	</div>
	
</div><!-- .page -->

